Law texts

The texts in this repository are Sindh Acts and Ordinances as codified, in English, by the Law, Parliamentary Affairs
and Criminal Prosecution Department, Government of Sindh, on the Sindh Code (sindhlaws.gov.pk, "Codified Laws").
Each codified PDF gives the law as updated till the date its page states. The site's footer reads: "(c) 2026 Law,
Parliamentary Affairs & Criminal Prosecution Department, Government of Sindh. All Rights Reserved." The site states
no licence and no terms of use, and no prohibition of reproduction.

- Copyright: the Copyright Ordinance, 1962 (Ordinance No. XXXIV of 1962), section 57(1), says "The following acts
  shall not constitute an infringement of copyright, namely:" and, in clause (q), "the reproduction or publication
  of__ (i) any matter which has been published in any official Gazette, or the report of any committee, commission,
  council, board or other like body appointed by the Government unless the reproduction or publication of such matter
  or report is prohibited by the Government". The Sindh Acts and Ordinances, and the laws amending them, are
  published in the Sindh Government Gazette; no prohibition of reproducing them was found.
- The limits of that basis: the codification itself (merging the amendments into the text, and the wording of the
  footnotes) is the department's work and was not itself published in the Gazette, so s. 57(1)(q)(i) does not in terms
  cover it; under sections 2 and 22 of the Ordinance a Government work carries copyright. The footnotes record facts
  (which law changed which words). The texts are reproduced without change to their wording; only the arrangement
  (one file per section, one paragraph per line, the marginal note as the heading line) is Lexifina's.
- The codified PDFs are not the authoritative text: the Acts and Ordinances as published in the Sindh Government
  Gazette are.

